  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local conflict prevention and access to justice support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is designed to address the current tensions ongoing in two payams of Alek South and North in Gogrial West county of warrap state.The project also will support and create awareness raising on Human Rights and protection issues in 5 payams of Kuac North,Kuac South,Gogrial,Alek North and South. The activities will be implemented through access to justice for the vulnerable groups in 5 payams mentioned above. The project propose to establish mechanisms of community dialogues with neighbouring communities of Gogrial East and Jur River counties who are in conflict with section of Aguok in Alek payams. Formation and training of Peace committees, formation and training of paralegal committees. These activities will target especially cattle camps youth who are engage in most of these violent conflicts through cattle raiding and revenge attacks, chiefs, women, spiritual leaders and local authorities such payam administrators and county commissioner who will be involved during the mobilization stages.</narrative>
  </description>
